From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 14:24:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Settings: do not poll VoNR on a radio that predates NR

Opening SIM settings ANRs on msm8992. NrAdvancedCallingPreferenceController.init() creates its
TelephonyCallback before any capability check, and onStart() registers it whenever it is non-null,
so the callback runs even though getAvailabilityStatus() has already decided the preference is
CONDITIONALLY_UNAVAILABLE. On the next call-state change it does
onCallStateChanged -> updateState -> isChecked -> TelephonyManager.isVoNrEnabled().

PhoneInterfaceManager.isVoNrEnabled hands the request to the phone's main thread and waits on its
MainThreadRequest monitor with no timeout. A 2016 RIL has no IS_VONR_ENABLED to answer, so nothing
completes the request: the binder thread waits forever, Settings' UI thread blocks behind it, and
further binder threads pile up in the same wait. Confirmed from the ANR trace, with
mHas5gCapability logged false on this device.

Guard both the registration and isChecked(). This only affects devices with no NR in their
supported radio access family, where the preference was already unavailable, so nothing that could
work is turned off.
---
 .../NrAdvancedCallingPreferenceController.java     | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/com/android/settings/network/telephony/NrAdvancedCallingPreferenceController.java b/src/com/android/settings/network/telephony/NrAdvancedCallingPreferenceController.java
index b585ecec6a..fe630b52db 100644
--- a/src/com/android/settings/network/telephony/NrAdvancedCallingPreferenceController.java
+++ b/src/com/android/settings/network/telephony/NrAdvancedCallingPreferenceController.java
@@ -125,6 +125,15 @@ public class NrAdvancedCallingPreferenceController extends TelephonyTogglePrefer
         if (mTelephonyCallback == null) {
             return;
         }
+        if (!mHas5gCapability) {
+            // Nothing to watch for: without NR this controller is CONDITIONALLY_UNAVAILABLE, and
+            // the callback's only job is to re-read a VoNR setting that cannot apply. Registering
+            // anyway means onCallStateChanged -> updateState -> isChecked -> isVoNrEnabled() on the
+            // main thread, and on a radio that predates NR the RIL never answers
+            // IS_VONR_ENABLED: PhoneInterfaceManager.sendRequest waits on its MainThreadRequest
+            // monitor with no timeout, so the binder thread never returns and Settings ANRs.
+            return;
+        }
         mTelephonyCallback.register(mTelephonyManager);
     }
 
@@ -162,6 +171,11 @@ public class NrAdvancedCallingPreferenceController extends TelephonyTogglePrefer
 
     @Override
     public boolean isChecked() {
+        if (!mHas5gCapability) {
+            // Belt and braces for the same blocking call: isChecked() is also reached from the
+            // ordinary preference path, and isVoNrEnabled() cannot be answered by a pre-NR RIL.
+            return false;
+        }
         return mTelephonyManager.isVoNrEnabled();
     }
 
